&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp&#39;s Point of Sale (POS) solution helps cafes, shops, bars, hair salons, and thousands of other businesses manage their day-to-day operations. Alongside the POS experience, merchants rely on powerful reporting, sales management, and fiscalisation tools to understand their business, stay compliant, and operate with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role would own these three domains from a design perspective - Reporting, Sales, and Fiscalisation. You&#39;ll design the experiences merchants use to analyse performance, manage sales activity, and navigate local fiscal requirements, while helping shape a more unified reporting experience across SumUp&#39;s payments, banking, and commerce products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with product managers, engineers, and data teams within POS, and collaborate with designers and stakeholders across SumUp to deliver experiences that are clear, trustworthy, and built to scale.&lt;/p&g

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(Senior) People Development Partner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;People Development&amp;nbsp; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;📍Berlin - on-site&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp University is how we build a culture of continuous learning across the business, running leadership programmes, workshops, and development initiatives for SumUppers in every market except Brazil. As part of a small, Berlin based team, you&#39;ll take ownership of flagship learning programmes and step in as a trusted facilitator, helping leaders and teams build the skills they need to do their best work. With demand for learning and development growing fast across SumUp, you&#39;ll have real scope to shape how programmes are delivered, grow your own facilitation craft, and work directly with teams in Berlin and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Order Taking squad owns core ordering experiences within SumUp’s Point of Sale app, including the shopping bag, checkout, the catalog experience within ordering, open orders, table management and printer integrations. These capabilities help thousands of hospitality merchants manage orders reliably during daily service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior iOS Engineer, you’ll build new hospitality workflows and evolve established ordering experiences across iOS and Android. You’ll work with SwiftUI on the platform-specific UI and contribute to shared Kotlin Multiplatform business logic. The role involves complex mobile engineering across multi-device synchronisation, shared order state and a large, established application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a small, experienced and fast-moving squad that works collaboratively through technical refinement, code reviews and pair programming. The team values engineers

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join one of the teams within SumUp’s Identity Lifecycle Mission, working on some of the most critical building blocks behind the merchant journey, from onboarding and identity verification to KYC/KYB, regulatory data collection, and managing customer identity throughout the entire lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, many of these capabilities live across different flows, legacy services, and tightly coupled integrations. We’re on a journey to bring these pieces together into a more coherent, scalable platform, with shared data models, reusable services, and clear ownership boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Backend Engineer, you won’t just be maintaining existing systems. You’ll have the opportunity to shape how our identity platform evolves, modernise critical services, and help build foundations that can support new regulations, markets, and product requirements without reinventing the wheel ever

&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Global Bank team &lt;/strong&gt;builds the core infrastructure and services that give merchants a digital bank account, helping small businesses manage their money easily and reliably.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
